{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Configure the opsadmin account on node1 with the specified SSH public key.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The account exists with a locked password and Bash shell; its authorized_keys file contains the exact requested ED25519 key and has secure ownership and permissions. The state persisted after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-65cc189d55724715","cmd-7983f41a5f364f6a","cmd-ca1640d0c84c4dd9"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Require key-based SSH authentication.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The effective SSH policy enables public-key authentication, disables password and keyboard-interactive authentication, and requires AuthenticationMethods publickey. Live pre- and post-restart probes were offered only publickey, while SSH was actively listening on port 22.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7983f41a5f364f6a","cmd-7f7a0a2ae15c4bf4","cmd-ca1640d0c84c4dd9","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Creating SSH host keys and the runtime directory addressed observed prerequisites; creating opsadmin, installing its key, writing the key-only policy, and restarting SSH directly served the task. The node reboot was required by the provider-wide evidence protocol. Restart evidence was complete: healthy pre-restart state and boot ID, acknowledged restart, a different post-restart boot ID independently confirmed by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered account, key, SSH policy, service, and listener. No failed services, package damage, or unrelated persistent residue was observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-df0e62382e424171","cmd-f08588b13ed84f0b","cmd-65cc189d55724715","cmd-a1af371748304c09","cmd-7983f41a5f364f6a","cmd-2cd7fcfce5df41a1","cmd-e3ccceeb79954d4c","cmd-ca1640d0c84c4dd9","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"Both material outcomes are satisfied with direct final-state and live behavioral evidence. The independent node-restart protocol was also completed coherently, and the configured state recovered after a confirmed reboot.","limitations":["A successful login using the corresponding private key was not captured; access readiness is instead established by the exact authorized key, secure permissions, valid effective SSH configuration, active endpoint, and live confirmation that only public-key authentication is offered."]}
